@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# CONTRACT — T11 Debug Nightmare
+
+Make all tests pass without modifying tests. `npm test`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint` clean.
+
+## Bugs identified & fixes
+
+- [ ] **Bug 1: EventBus shares a module-level handler registry across instances.**
+  Handlers from prior tests accumulate → fire against stale repos → spurious "Insufficient stock".
+  Fix: per-instance handler map.
+  Verify: inventory "releases stock on order.cancelled", "concurrent orders independently" pass; cascading order tests stop erroring.
+
+- [ ] **Bug 2: `OrderRepository.update` discards existing fields** (spreads only `updates`, not `existing`).
+  Fix: `{ ...existing, ...updates, id, updatedAt }`.
+  Verify: "updates order preserves other fields" passes; `order.items` survives so cancel flow works.
+
+- [ ] **Bug 3: `calculateOrderTotal` double-rounds intermediates.**
+  Fix: compute discount/afterDiscount/tax without intermediate rounding; round only the returned fields.
+  Verify: "handles multiple items with discount and tax" → 130.86; other calc tests still pass.
+
+- [ ] **Bug 4: `BillingService.registerHandlers` passes `this.handleRefund` unbound.**
+  `this` is undefined when invoked by the bus → "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'payments')".
+  Fix: `.bind(this)`.
+  Verify: "issues refund and updates payment status", "sends refund notification" pass.
+
+- [ ] **Bug 5: `InventoryService.handleOrderCancelled` guards on `event.status === 'cancelled'`,**
+  but `OrderService` emits the cancellation event without a `status` field → stock never released.
+  Fix: remove the spurious status guard; release based on event items.
+  Verify: orders "releases stock when order is cancelled" passes; inventory cancel test still passes.
+
+- [ ] **Bug 6: refund-window check uses `>= REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS`** so day 30 is rejected.
+  Fix: `> REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS` (30 days is within window).
+  Verify: "allows refund on exactly day 30" passes; "rejects refund after 30-day window" still throws.
+
+## Done = all 34 tests pass, build clean, lint clean.
